<Article title="Privacy Policy · Stillread" heading="Privacy Policy" eyebrow="Effective October 19, 2026" description="Stillread doesn't collect your data. Your notes stay on your Mac, and the app has no analytics or tracking.">
    <Summary slot="summary">
        <p class="font-semibold">The short version: Stillread doesn't collect any of your data.</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-ink-soft">Your notes are read on your Mac and never leave it. There are no accounts, no analytics, no ads and no tracking in the app. The only time Stillread contacts anyone on your behalf is to check a licence key with Polar, our payment provider, and to check for updates.</p>
    </Summary>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>Stillread is made by Cascadia Digital Inc. ("we", "us"), in British Columbia, Canada. This policy explains what information the Stillread Mac app, its Quick Look preview and this website use, and how.</p>

    <h2>Your notes and files</h2>
    <p>Stillread opens the files and folders you choose and shows them on your Mac. When you edit a note, it's saved back to the same file on your Mac. Your files are never uploaded, copied to us, or shared with anyone. The Quick Look preview works the same way, entirely on your Mac.</p>
    <p>The app keeps a few settings on your Mac, such as your typeface, text size and recently opened folders. You can clear recent folders from the File menu, and deleting Stillread's settings removes them.</p>

    <h2>Images from the web</h2>
    <p>If a note includes an image hosted on a website, Stillread loads that image from the website, the same way a browser would. That website may see your IP address. Everything else on the page, including diagrams and code highlighting, is drawn on your Mac.</p>

    <h2>Buying and activating Editing</h2>
    <p>Editing is sold through <a href="https://polar.sh">Polar</a>, which acts as the merchant of record. When you buy, Polar collects your name, email address and payment details to process the payment and send your licence key. We receive your name, email address and order details from Polar so we can help with support and refunds. We never see your full card details. Polar handles this information under <a href="https://polar.sh/legal/privacy">its privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <p>When you enter your licence key, Stillread sends Polar exactly three things: the key, a random activation ID made up on your Mac when you activate (it isn't your Mac's name, serial number or any hardware identifier), and Stillread's version number. Polar uses these to confirm the key and count your activations (up to 2 Macs). The activation is saved in your Mac's Keychain.</p>
    <p>About once a day, while Stillread is open, it sends the key and activation ID to Polar again to confirm the licence is still active. Choosing <strong>Deactivate This Mac</strong> in Settings sends them once more to free that Mac. Nothing about your notes or files is ever sent.</p>

    <h2>Updates</h2>
    <p>Stillread asks before it starts checking for updates automatically, and you can change that later. Each check downloads a small file from stillread.app. The request includes Stillread's version number and, like any web request, your IP address, which our host may keep in short-lived server logs. It doesn't send any other information about your Mac or your notes. Updates themselves download from downloads.stillread.app, which is served by Cloudflare.</p>
    <p>When you download Stillread or an update, we count it. A count records only the file name, the day, and whether it came from this website or from the app's updater. No IP address or other information about you is stored.</p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>This website (stillread.app) is hosted by Netlify, which keeps standard server logs. We use <a href="https://usefathom.com/privacy">Fathom Analytics</a> to count visits. Fathom doesn't use cookies, doesn't collect personal information, and doesn't track you across other websites. We only see totals, like how many people visited a page or clicked Download.</p>

    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>If you email us, we use your message and address only to reply and help you. We don't add you to a mailing list.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Stillread doesn't collect personal information from anyone, including children under 13.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, we'll update this page and the effective date above. If Stillread ever starts collecting data, we'll update this policy before that change ships.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about privacy? Email <SupportEmail />.</p>
</Article>
